From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abhishek Sahu <abhsahu@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 10:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: platform/arm64: nvidia-ffa-ec: suppress driver
 bind/unbind

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167300

The FF-A bridge and its EC subunits are a single firmware fixture on
the systems this driver targets:

  * They expose the ACPI FFH region handler that consumer ACPI devices
    depend on for the life of the system.
  * There is no way to re-create the FFH region or the EC secure
    services once torn down.
  * The driver is built-in only (NVIDIA_FFA_EC is bool, depends on
    ARM_FFA_TRANSPORT=y), so module removal is not possible.

There are two live-runtime ways for the .remove callbacks of the three
in-tree drivers (nvidia_ffa_driver, nvidia_ffa_ec_service_driver,
nvidia_ffa_control_service_driver) to fire:

  * sysfs bind/unbind of one of these drivers themselves, via
    /sys/bus/{platform,arm_ffa}/drivers/<name>/{bind,unbind}. This is
    an admin-triggered debug/test path that has no legitimate use for a
    firmware fixture the whole platform depends on.

  * sysfs unbind of the upstream ARM FF-A core platform driver at
    /sys/bus/platform/drivers/arm-ffa/unbind. ffa_remove() cleans up
    notifications and unregisters every ffa_device, cascading .remove
    into our two arm_ffa-bus drivers (nvidia_ffa_ec_service_driver and
    nvidia_ffa_control_service_driver). It does not invoke
    nvidia_ffa_remove() -- that is the separate NVIDIA platform_driver
    callback, and the FFH region handler is installed and torn down
    there. After the arm-ffa core is unbound the FFH region handler
    therefore stays installed, but the EC service list has been
    emptied, so any subsequent FFH access returns -ENODEV rather than
    reaching a live SP. We cannot suppress the arm-ffa-core bind attr
    from here; the FF-A core does not set suppress_bind_attrs and that
    is upstream policy, not ours to change.

Set driver.suppress_bind_attrs = true on all three of our drivers to
remove sysfs unbind of this driver as an admin-triggerable teardown
path. The arm-ffa-core unbind path is unaffected, but it drains its
own notification workqueue (destroy_workqueue() in
ffa_notifications_cleanup()) before invoking our .remove callbacks --
by the time our .remove runs on that path, no callback can still be
in flight, so it cannot trigger the teardown races that the earlier
patches contain. Those races require .remove to run while the FF-A
notification workqueue is still dispatching, and the sysfs unbind of
our own driver is now the only path that would leave that window
open.

Signed-off-by: Abhishek Sahu <abhsahu@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Jamie Nguyen <jamien@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit 73defabbe73683280c7b4c630c3df19a8eea3415 resolute:linux-nvidia-bos)
Signed-off-by: Jacob Martin <jacob.martin@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00652
Ledger-Origin: nvidia@01f6e542f28b5deff6569210985e215ff0e222f2
---
 drivers/platform/arm64/nvidia-ffa-ec.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/arm64/nvidia-ffa-ec.c b/drivers/platform/arm64/nvidia-ffa-ec.c
index c22e835b84ef..92834fd332bb 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/arm64/nvidia-ffa-ec.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/arm64/nvidia-ffa-ec.c
@@ -1017,6 +1017,9 @@ static struct ffa_driver nvidia_ffa_ec_service_driver = {
 	.probe = nvidia_ffa_ec_service_probe,
 	.remove = nvidia_ffa_ec_service_remove,
 	.id_table = nvidia_ffa_ec_service_ids,
+	.driver = {
+		.suppress_bind_attrs = true,
+	},
 };
 
 /*
@@ -1077,6 +1080,9 @@ static struct ffa_driver nvidia_ffa_control_service_driver = {
 	.probe = nvidia_ffa_control_service_probe,
 	.remove = nvidia_ffa_control_service_remove,
 	.id_table = nvidia_ffa_control_service_ids,
+	.driver = {
+		.suppress_bind_attrs = true,
+	},
 };
 
 static const struct acpi_device_id nvidia_ffa_device_ids[] = {
@@ -1158,6 +1164,7 @@ static struct platform_driver nvidia_ffa_driver = {
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "nvidia-ffa",
 		.acpi_match_table = nvidia_ffa_device_ids,
+		.suppress_bind_attrs = true,
 	},
 };
 
